    {
      "id": "f4f47981-3b71-4c32-9afd-ffe5c787640a",
      "name": "Why the Model Context Protocol Is Awesome",
      "path": "WWW / The MCP Blog / Why the Model Context Protocol Is Awesome",
      "docTypeId": "ce9277d4-0f4b-44cb-b319-8338454cdd66",
      "templateId": "abfcaba9-7576-40b4-a775-06f187f6c033",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "summary",
          "value": "One open standard between AI agents and the tools they use — and why it changes how software gets built."
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.DateTime",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "publishDate",
          "value": "2026-10-08 00:00:00"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "blocks",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": null,
                  "rowSpan": null,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "731e69af-5201-4e21-aa19-a46d6969eef3",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": null,
                  "rowSpan": null,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "3325d2e2-dea8-49e8-b892-5582faa01ab4",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": null,
                  "rowSpan": null,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "0a53c807-5e14-415c-92ef-de7f90696589",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": null,
                  "rowSpan": null,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "69c4b315-0248-427e-a7cd-c9d24e052e6c",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "a6020ea9-c321-4985-b3f5-a16410cb5493",
                "key": "731e69af-5201-4e21-aa19-a46d6969eef3",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "heading",
                    "value": "Why the Model Context Protocol Is Awesome"
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "subheading",
                    "value": "One standard between agents and tools — and it changes how software gets built."
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "backgroundImage",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "e9e9533d-3073-4546-9ed4-c2937565c646",
                        "mediaKey": "cc2a4e4b-3f2b-4bfd-8958-76acc39ca3e9",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "06389e85-f308-467f-9f48-2ae1b3fe07dd",
                "key": "3325d2e2-dea8-49e8-b892-5582faa01ab4",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "body",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>MCP — the Model Context Protocol — is what lets an AI agent actually <em>do</em> things in the real world: read your files, query your database, drive your CMS, post to your chat. Before MCP, every one of those integrations was a bespoke adapter, written twice — once for the tool, once for the model. MCP replaces all of that with a single open standard.</p><h2>One protocol, every tool</h2><p>A tool server speaks MCP once, and every MCP-capable client — Claude, Cursor, your own scripts — can use it. Write the server, get the whole ecosystem. It is the same network effect that made HTTP and USB win, applied to agent tooling.</p><ul><li><strong>Tools</strong> — functions the agent can call, with typed schemas.</li><li><strong>Resources</strong> — read-only data the agent can browse, like files or records.</li><li><strong>Prompts</strong> — reusable prompt templates a server shares with its clients.</li></ul>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "40471ceb-3ed3-4c2c-ac14-da1c604ed2ed",
                "key": "0a53c807-5e14-415c-92ef-de7f90696589",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "8d43b989-2b49-48e0-b1f1-aeeac3275604",
                        "mediaKey": "45bd01bc-5c41-4a9e-88c7-82156a29f850",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "caption",
                    "value": "Where the agent does the typing. Photo by Christopher Gower on Unsplash."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "06389e85-f308-467f-9f48-2ae1b3fe07dd",
                "key": "69c4b315-0248-427e-a7cd-c9d24e052e6c",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "body",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<h2>Your agent, your rules</h2><p>Because the client is the one calling the tools, <em>you</em> stay in control: every call is visible, every permission can be scoped, and nothing happens unless the agent asks. MCP turns \"the AI did something\" into \"the AI asked, and I said yes\".</p><p>And because the protocol is JSON-based and transport-agnostic, it works the same whether the server runs on your laptop over stdio or in the cloud over HTTP. Local dev and production are the same code.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "731e69af-5201-4e21-aa19-a46d6969eef3",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
